{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "MAT.3.ASW"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/MAT/3-b934748aa772b8a4b248e0d5876467e5.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/MAT/3-b934748aa772b8a4b248e0d5876467e5.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}, {"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1668/32k/MAT/3-09d56d347b6e0ad8098f957870647c59.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1668/m4a/32k/MAT/3-09d56d347b6e0ad8098f957870647c59.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1668, "version_id": 59, "title": "Living Water Bible - ESV Music Project by Lutheran Bible Translators", "timing_available": false, "dramatized": true, "default": false}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bkMAT\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch3\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3\">\n            <div class=\"label\">3</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">John the Baptist Prepares the Way</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 1-12, see Mark 1:2-8; Luke 3:2-17   </span></span><span class=\"content\">In those days </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 1:6, 7 </span></span><span class=\"content\">John the Baptist came preaching in </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Josh. 15:61; [Judg. 1:16]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the wilderness of Judea, </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 4:17; Mark 1:15 </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Repent, for </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:7; Dan. 2:44; [ch. 6:10]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the kingdom of heaven is at hand.&#8221;</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">3:2 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">the kingdom of heaven has come near</span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">For this is he who was spoken of by the prophet Isaiah when he said,</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.3\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        John 1:23; Cited from Isa. 40:3   </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;The voice of one crying in the wilderness:</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.3\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Luke 1:76\n        </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8216;Prepare</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">3:3 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">crying: Prepare in the wilderness</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> the way of the Lord;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.3\"><span class=\"content\">make his paths straight.&#8217;&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"m\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.3\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">Now John wore </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Kgs. 1:8; Zech. 13:4; [Heb. 11:37] </span></span><span class=\"content\">a garment of camel&#8217;s hair and a leather belt around his waist, and his food was </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Lev. 11:22 </span></span><span class=\"content\">locusts and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">1 Sam. 14:26</span></span><span class=\"content\">wild honey. </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">Then Jerusalem and all Judea and all the region about the Jordan were going out to him, </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"content\">and they were baptized by him in the river Jordan, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 19:18</span></span><span class=\"content\">confessing their sins.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.6\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">But when he saw many of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 23:13, 15 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the Pharisees and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 22:23 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Sadducees coming to his baptism, he said to them, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:34; 23:33 </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;You brood of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 140:3 </span></span><span class=\"content\">vipers! Who warned you to flee from </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 5:9; Eph. 5:6; Col. 3:6; 1 Thess. 1:10</span></span><span class=\"content\">the wrath to come? </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">Bear fruit </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 26:20</span></span><span class=\"content\">in keeping with repentance. </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">And do not presume to say to yourselves, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 8:39 </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8216;We have Abraham as our father,&#8217; for I tell you, God is able from </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 4:3]</span></span><span class=\"content\">these stones to raise up children for Abraham. </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"content\">Even now the axe is laid to the root of the trees. </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 7:19; Luke 13:7, 9; John 15:2, 6</span></span><span class=\"content\">Every tree therefore that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.10\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        John 1:26; Acts 1:5   </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;I baptize you with water </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 13:24; 19:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">for repentance, but </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 1:15, 27; 3:30, 31; Acts 13:25 </span></span><span class=\"content\">he who is coming after me is mightier than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to carry. He will baptize you </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 1:33; Acts 11:16 </span></span><span class=\"content\">with the Holy Spirit and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Isa. 4:4; Mal. 3:2, 3; Acts 2:3]</span></span><span class=\"content\">fire. </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"content\">His </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Isa. 30:24 </span></span><span class=\"content\">winnowing fork is in his hand, and he will clear his threshing floor and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 13:30 </span></span><span class=\"content\">gather his wheat into the barn, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Mal. 4:1 </span></span><span class=\"content\">but the chaff he will burn with </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Mark 9:43, 48</span></span><span class=\"content\">unquenchable fire.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Baptism of Jesus</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.12\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 13-17, see Mark 1:9-11; Luke 3:21, 22; [John 1:32-34]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Then Jesus came </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 2:22</span></span><span class=\"content\">from Galilee to the Jordan to John, to be baptized by him. </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[John 13:6]</span></span><span class=\"content\">John would have prevented him, saying, &#8220;I need to be baptized by you, and do you come to me?&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"content\">But Jesus answered him, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Let it be so now, for thus it is fitting for us to fulfill all righteousness.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\"> Then he consented. </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"content\">And when Jesus was baptized, immediately he went up from the water, and behold, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 7:56 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the heavens were opened to him,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">3:16 </span><span class=\"ft\">Some manuscripts omit </span><span class=\"fq\">to him</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> and he </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 1:32, 33; [Luke 4:18, 21; Acts 10:38]</span></span><span class=\"content\">saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and coming to rest on him; </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"MAT.3.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"content\">and behold, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 12:28 </span></span><span class=\"content\">a voice from heaven said, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 17:5; 2 Pet. 1:17; [Ps. 2:7; Isa. 42:1; Eph. 1:6; Col. 1:13; 1 John 5:9]</span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;This is my beloved Son,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">3:17 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">my Son, my </span><span class=\"ft\">(or </span><span class=\"fq\">the</span><span class=\"ft\">) </span><span class=\"fq\">Beloved</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> with whom I am well pleased.&#8221;</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["MAT.4"], "human": "Matthew 4", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "previous": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["MAT.2"], "human": "Matthew 2", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "reference": {"usfm": ["MAT.3"], "human": "Matthew 3", "version_id": 59}}, "usfm": "MAT.3.ASW", "locale": "en", "versionData": {"audio": true, "copyright_short": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Cros